<p>A problem by Russian mathematician Viktor Prasolov:</p>
<p>A circle is divided by points into 3<em>k</em> arcs such that there are <em>k</em> arcs each of length 1, 2, and 3. Prove that two of the division points are diametrically opposite one another.</p>

